# Coding Patterns

- **Pure core, I/O at the edges:** core classes are static and take plain inputs (`ExportContext`, `JsonElement`, paths). Planning is separated from writing (`ExportWriter.Plan` vs `ExportWriter.Apply`) so behavior can be tested and previewed (`--dry-run`, `--check`).
- **Result records instead of exceptions** for expected problems: validation returns `ContextValidationResult` (errors, warnings, profile); the CLI maps it to output and exit codes.
- **One table of targets:** adding an export target means adding one entry to `ExportTargets.All` plus its title in `ContextExporter`, not editing the CLI.
- **Scoped content lives in `.aicontext/rules/`**, not in the CLI or in tool-specific files. Test conventions are an example: see `rules/tests.md`.
